"},{"Math":{"src":"F^2"}},{"Text":", "},{"Math":{"src":"G^2"}},{"Text":" and the associators."}]}}]}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"A lax natural transformation is "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"pseudonatural"}]},{"Text":" when every "},{"Math":{"src":"sigma_f"}},{"Text":" is invertible. As with "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"pseudofunctor","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"pseudofunctors"}]}},{"Text":", this is a property, so the pseudonatural transformations "},{"Math":{"src":"F => G"}},{"Text":" are a full subcategory of the category of lax transformations and "},{"Span":{"role":"","attrs":[],"body":[{"Text":"modifications"}]}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Between "},{"Span":{"role":"","attrs":[],"body":[{"Text":"prestacks"}]}},{"Text":" the 1-cells are taken to be pseudonatural. The reason is biuniversality: a transformation whose components "},{"Math":{"src":"sigma_x"}},{"Text":" are all equivalences of categories is an equivalence of prestacks only if its naturality cells are invertible, and a "},{"Span":{"role":"","attrs":[],"body":[{"Text":"biuniversal element"}]}},{"Text":" should be exactly a representation of a prestack up to such an equivalence."}]}]}}}]}}
